<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Pictones</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.) · capital Lemonum</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Gallic people of Poitou who built ships for Caesar against the Veneti and gave their name to Poitiers and Poitou.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Pictones held the land south of the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a>, around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poitiers">Lemonum</a> (Poitiers), with a coastline on the Atlantic. They were among the larger peoples of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Caesar used their shipyards in 56 BCE for the fleet that defeated the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/veneti">Veneti</a>. Their leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duratius">Duratius</a> remained loyal to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, which split the people during the revolts.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 51 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duratius">Duratius</a> was besieged in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poitiers">Lemonum</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dumnacus">Dumnacus</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/andecavi">Andecavi</a> until Roman forces relieved him. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> Lemonum, later called Pictavi, became Poitiers, a major city and bishopric, and the region kept the name <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-poitou">Poitou</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/pictones.jpg" alt="Pictones" width="320" height="318"><figcaption>Image: World Imaging · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pictones_coin_depicting_warrior_5th_to_1st_century_BCE.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Lemonum</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Duratius</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Pictavi</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-176&amp;focus=pictones" aria-label="Pictones on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4729 563 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Pictones lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5049 819h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5049 819h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day France. <a href="/atlas?year=-176&amp;focus=pictones">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

